### Visits Data Model

Source: https://github.com/514-labs/moosestack/blob/main/apps/framework-docs-v2/content/moosestack/apis/semantic-layer.mdx

Defines the structure of a visit record, including fields like studio ID, user ID, status, and dates. This model is used for querying attendance and booking data.

```APIDOC
## Visits Data Model

### Description
A booking or attendance record for a class at a fitness studio.

### Fields
- **id** (Key<number>) - Unique identifier for the visit.
- **studio_id** (number) - Tenant identifier. Every query must filter on this.
- **user_id** (number) - The client who booked the visit.
- **status** (number) - Status of the visit: 1 = attended, 2 = no-show, 3 = late cancel, 4 = early cancel.
- **start_date** (Date) - Scheduled start time of the class. Primary time dimension for queries.
- **created_at** (Date) - Timestamp when the visit record was created.

### TypeScript Example
```typescript
interface Visit {
  id: Key<number>;
  studio_id: number;
  user_id: number;
  status: number;
  start_date: Date;
  created_at: Date;
}

export const VisitsTable = new OlapTable<Visit>("visits", {
  orderByFields: ["studio_id", "start_date", "id"],
});
```

### Python Example
```python
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field
from moose_lib import Key, OlapTable, OlapConfig
from datetime import datetime

class Visit(BaseModel):
    id: Key[int]
    studio_id: int = Field(description="Tenant identifier. Every query must filter on this.")
    user_id: int = Field(description="The client who booked the visit.")
    status: int = Field(description="1 = attended, 2 = no-show, 3 = late cancel, 4 = early cancel")
    start_date: datetime = Field(description="Scheduled start time of the class.")
    created_at: datetime

VisitsTable = OlapTable[Visit]("visits", OlapConfig(
    order_by_fields=["studio_id", "start_date", "id"],
))
```
